{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q005_cupredoxin_function_transfer","answer":"SCOPe 2.08 places all three in the Cupredoxins superfamily b.6.1 (SUNID 49503), within the Cupredoxin-like fold b.6 (49502) and All beta proteins class b (48724), but in distinct families: Plastocyanin/azurin-like b.6.1.1 (49504), Ephrin ectodomain b.6.1.5 (74874), and Peptidylarginine deiminase Pad4, N-terminal domain b.6.1.6 (110107). Thus SCOPe proposes an evolutionary relationship at superfamily level, beyond merely sharing a fold, without asserting close family-level relatedness. Fold membership alone describes structural similarity and does not establish homology; class membership is still broader.

The annotations explicitly qualify both ephrin ectodomains and the PAD4 N-terminal domain as probably related to cupredoxins but lacking the metal-binding site. Ephrin is identified as a eukaryotic signaling domain. These specific annotations limit the superfamily’s general copper-binding description: copper binding and electron transfer must not be transferred across all its families. Canonical plastocyanin and azurin are copper-dependent electron carriers; ephrins function as Eph-receptor ligands, while PAD4 is a calcium-dependent peptidylarginine deiminase whose catalytic activity resides in its C-terminal domain. Classification of PAD4’s N-terminal domain neither makes it an electron carrier nor assigns that domain the enzyme’s catalytic function.

A shared structural core can inform domain-level structural comparisons or template choice, but does not justify copying metal sites, binding interfaces, or biochemical annotations. Functional assignment requires target-specific evidence: conservation and three-dimensional geometry of copper-coordinating residues, direct metal-binding or spectroscopic evidence, and redox/electron-transfer measurements with appropriate partners. Sequence/profile evidence and detailed structural comparisons can strengthen homology inference, but cannot substitute for functional evidence.","evidence_used":["Pretrained model knowledge","mcp__scope__search_scop","mcp__scope__get_scop_node","mcp__scope__list_scop_children","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=Cupredoxin&mode=auto&limit=30","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=PAD4&mode=auto&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49503","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49503/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49503/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/b.6.1/children?limit=30","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/74874/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110107/annotations"]}]}
